{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"THIRD OCCURRENCE, and a detail that narrows the mechanism — 2026-08-13, `macos-latest py3.13` shard only, every ubuntu shard green each time.\n\nOccurrences today:\n1. Gerrit **1715** (event_append split; `src/rebar/_store/` only) — run 31680986340.\n2. Gerrit **1716** (rich-text conflict-safety pins, story `disparaged-parodistic-shrew`; TESTS-ONLY, one new file) — run 31681638153.\n3. Gerrit **1716** again, after a recheck — run 31683437250.\n\nAll three: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`, failing at\n`assert any(\"declined 1 inbound link removal\" in m for m in messages)`.\n\n**The narrowing detail: the captured records are not EMPTY — they contain the per-link decline line, and only the pass-SUMMARY line is missing.** In run 1 the captured line named link `1bc5-25e4-0ebd-44e0 -> e727-b3b4-02ff-4972`; in run 3 it named `dd93-74a0-7669-4b1e -> 5d49-b6b2-1725-4a23`. Different ids across runs, same shape.\n\nTwo things follow:\n- The capture is LIVE and working when the per-link record is emitted, so this is not a caplog handler that was never attached. Something happens between the per-link emission and the later summary emission — a propagation/handler swap, or the summary being emitted under a different logger or after the fixture's capture scope ends.\n- The differing link ids show the test body genuinely re-runs with fresh data each time, so the failure is not a stale-state artifact; it is ordering or timing.\n\nRecheck is NOT being attempted a fourth time on 1716 per operator instruction — it will be rebased over the fix once this lands. Flagging that this is now blocking a change that cannot possibly reach the assertion (1716 adds one test file and touches no production code), so the flake is costing throughput on unrelated lanes, not just noise."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786612750795210001,"uuid":"dd297931-184a-46ab-99ca-c1de03108809"}